WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:01.111
- Good morning, Believe Nation.

00:00:01.111 --> 00:00:02.409
My name is Evan Carmichael.

00:00:02.409 --> 00:00:05.340
My one word is believe and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:05.340 --> 00:00:08.022
will solve all of the
world's major problems.

00:00:08.022 --> 00:00:09.077
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:09.077 --> 00:00:13.778
today's message is it doesn't
matter what your mom thinks.

00:00:13.778 --> 00:00:15.427
Over to you Eckhart Tolle.

00:00:15.427 --> 00:00:17.258
(rooster crowing)

00:00:17.258 --> 00:00:20.429
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:00:20.429 --> 00:00:23.033
♫ Entspresso keep my going.

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:27.268
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:00:27.268 --> 00:00:28.868
- You get unhappy, if you.

00:00:28.868 --> 00:00:31.921
For many years, before
I wrote The Power of Now

00:00:31.921 --> 00:00:33.222
and it became successful.

00:00:33.222 --> 00:00:37.156
I was basically a failure
in the eyes of the world.

00:00:37.156 --> 00:00:39.315
So he's already almost 50.

00:00:39.315 --> 00:00:41.145
And what has he achieved?

00:00:41.145 --> 00:00:43.990
My mom said, you have
thrown away your life.

00:00:43.990 --> 00:00:46.426
You had so many
possibilities in your life.

00:00:46.426 --> 00:00:49.059
You walked out of graduate
school in Cambridge.

00:00:49.059 --> 00:00:51.559
Why did you walk out of there?

00:00:53.095 --> 00:00:56.165
My mom, and many other
people said this person

00:00:56.165 --> 00:00:57.509
has failed in life.

00:00:57.509 --> 00:01:01.664
He has no job, he has
no insurance policies.

00:01:01.664 --> 00:01:02.760
Nothing.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.895
No pension plan.

00:01:04.895 --> 00:01:08.142
Just, almost nothing in the bank.

00:01:08.142 --> 00:01:09.447
Failure

00:01:09.447 --> 00:01:12.702
And then a few years later,
people bought The Power of Now

00:01:12.702 --> 00:01:14.785
and became a best seller.

00:01:15.670 --> 00:01:17.582
Now, a big success.

00:01:17.582 --> 00:01:21.524
Okay if I had derived
my identity at that time

00:01:21.524 --> 00:01:24.324
from what the world was telling me.

00:01:24.324 --> 00:01:26.842
Or my mind would have told
me if I had been listening

00:01:26.842 --> 00:01:29.890
to my mind, I would
have been very unhappy.

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:31.720
I didn't though.

00:01:31.720 --> 00:01:33.428
I was fine.

00:01:33.428 --> 00:01:37.009
Because my identity wasn't
derived from that anymore.

00:01:37.009 --> 00:01:40.662
And fortunately even when
in the eyes of the world,

00:01:40.662 --> 00:01:43.221
I suddenly became a success.

00:01:43.221 --> 00:01:45.699
I don't want to derive my
from identity from that.

00:01:45.699 --> 00:01:49.782
It's just a cheap substitute
for who I really am.

00:01:51.622 --> 00:01:55.539
The satisfaction that
comes is the satisfaction

00:01:57.332 --> 00:01:59.915
that the work that's happening.

00:02:01.487 --> 00:02:02.747
The teaching that's happening

00:02:02.747 --> 00:02:05.326
is transforming people's lives.

00:02:05.326 --> 00:02:07.000
That's very satisfying.

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:09.518
But I don't get any personal
satisfaction though.

00:02:09.518 --> 00:02:14.199
Because I don't feel that as
this separate me produced it.

00:02:14.199 --> 00:02:15.538
- It would be great to have the support

00:02:15.538 --> 00:02:18.051
of your mom, of your
parents, of your friends,

00:02:18.051 --> 00:02:19.557
of your family, of your community.

00:02:19.557 --> 00:02:21.998
To do whatever it is that you want to do.

00:02:21.998 --> 00:02:24.646
But their support shouldn't be reflective

00:02:24.646 --> 00:02:26.521
of whether you should
go up and do it or not.

00:02:26.521 --> 00:02:29.160
Like, if your mom says this is a bad idea

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:30.583
that means you're not going to do it?

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:31.416
You know.

00:02:31.416 --> 00:02:33.751
When you're growing up, when
you're five years old okay.

00:02:33.751 --> 00:02:36.231
Listen to your mom, do what she says.

00:02:36.231 --> 00:02:37.124
You get in trouble, right.

00:02:37.124 --> 00:02:39.069
But how old are you now?

00:02:39.069 --> 00:02:41.668
Like at some point you
decide, this is my life.

00:02:41.668 --> 00:02:43.904
And I would love to have
the support of my parents.

00:02:43.904 --> 00:02:46.748
And I had the support of my
parents while what I was doing.

00:02:46.748 --> 00:02:47.682
It was great.

00:02:47.682 --> 00:02:49.306
But if you don't have the support,

00:02:49.306 --> 00:02:50.567
at what point do you decide

00:02:50.567 --> 00:02:53.130
that you're an adult.

00:02:53.130 --> 00:02:55.529
You're going to do the
thing that you want to do.

00:02:55.529 --> 00:02:57.604
Are you going to be 40 years
old and still listening

00:02:57.604 --> 00:03:01.020
to your parents and what they see for you?

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:03.625
And a lot of times,
especially your parents,

00:03:03.625 --> 00:03:04.842
it's out of love.

00:03:04.842 --> 00:03:05.675
Right?

00:03:05.675 --> 00:03:07.036
They want you to be successful.

00:03:07.036 --> 00:03:09.607
They want you to have a great life.

00:03:09.607 --> 00:03:12.332
They just want you to
do it on their terms.

00:03:12.332 --> 00:03:15.662
The way that they see
success may not be lined up

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:18.178
with how you see success.

00:03:18.178 --> 00:03:19.726
And so they may not be
the ones telling you

00:03:19.726 --> 00:03:21.798
that you suck and you'll
never be anything.

00:03:21.798 --> 00:03:23.221
Though some parents are like that too.

00:03:23.221 --> 00:03:25.411
Which that's a whole nother story.

00:03:25.411 --> 00:03:28.251
But most of the time it's out of love.

00:03:28.251 --> 00:03:30.568
It's out of them wanting
to see you be successful.

00:03:30.568 --> 00:03:34.019
You just have different views
of what that looks like.

00:03:34.019 --> 00:03:36.422
And at some point you have to
decide that this is my life.

00:03:36.422 --> 00:03:37.850
I'm going to do things that I want to do.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:41.464
And if you judge your
self worth based only off

00:03:41.464 --> 00:03:45.547
of the results, then you're
never going to be happy.

00:03:46.705 --> 00:03:48.658
You're never going to feel valuable.

00:03:48.658 --> 00:03:49.491
Right?

00:03:49.491 --> 00:03:51.179
And so, I look at my Youtube videos.

00:03:51.179 --> 00:03:52.074
I look at this channel.

00:03:52.074 --> 00:03:53.494
Look at what I'm making for you guys.

00:03:53.494 --> 00:03:54.874
I love everything that I do.

00:03:54.874 --> 00:03:56.174
I love the process.

00:03:56.174 --> 00:03:58.450
This is why it's so important
that you love the process

00:03:58.450 --> 00:04:01.131
of the work and not just the results.

00:04:01.131 --> 00:04:04.016
It's not just about hittin
a million subscribers right?

00:04:04.016 --> 00:04:05.562
That's my goal for the new year.

00:04:05.562 --> 00:04:07.767
Have one million subscribers
let's see if we hit it.

00:04:07.767 --> 00:04:10.043
It's not just about hitting
a billion entrepreneurs.

00:04:10.043 --> 00:04:11.873
That's my lifetime goal.

00:04:11.873 --> 00:04:13.419
I want to have a big impact.

00:04:13.419 --> 00:04:15.296
I want to reach a billion entrepreneurs.

00:04:15.296 --> 00:04:18.595
If I can do that and even
have a half a percent impact

00:04:18.595 --> 00:04:20.948
on their life, all the things
that they're going to go off

00:04:20.948 --> 00:04:23.432
and make is going to be insane.

00:04:23.432 --> 00:04:26.479
And I'm honored to play a small tiny piece

00:04:26.479 --> 00:04:28.229
in your success.

00:04:28.229 --> 00:04:30.020
But it's not just about
hitting that number.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:32.748
Because you can have a
goal, you can have a target.

00:04:32.748 --> 00:04:34.384
And say I really want to reach this thing.

00:04:34.384 --> 00:04:36.668
I'll do anything to get there.

00:04:36.668 --> 00:04:39.020
But you won't do anything.

00:04:39.020 --> 00:04:40.527
And you shouldn't do anything.

00:04:40.527 --> 00:04:42.167
You can only force yourself
to do something you don't like

00:04:42.167 --> 00:04:43.953
for so long.

00:04:43.953 --> 00:04:45.661
You've got to do the work.

00:04:45.661 --> 00:04:48.419
That Jerry Seinfeld calls
the torture you can endure.

00:04:48.419 --> 00:04:49.398
The work that you love.

00:04:49.398 --> 00:04:51.511
The torture that you love.

00:04:51.511 --> 00:04:55.006
The process is more important
than hitting the goal.

00:04:55.006 --> 00:04:57.120
I was asked if I'm going to do a big party

00:04:57.120 --> 00:04:59.073
for hitting a million subscribers.

00:04:59.073 --> 00:05:00.495
And I don't know.

00:05:00.495 --> 00:05:02.161
Like, I do it more for you guys.

00:05:02.161 --> 00:05:03.217
Than for me.

00:05:03.217 --> 00:05:04.761
Right, we did one, we did a livestream

00:05:04.761 --> 00:05:06.795
at half a million.

00:05:06.795 --> 00:05:08.260
And I haven't done any other ones since.

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:10.173
We crossed a hundred million
views on the channel.

00:05:10.173 --> 00:05:11.392
Which is awesome.

00:05:11.392 --> 00:05:13.519
But once we've hit the
milestone, it's a great target

00:05:13.519 --> 00:05:14.352
to go and reach.

00:05:14.352 --> 00:05:17.189
But then it's in the past.

00:05:17.189 --> 00:05:19.095
I don't want to live in the past.

00:05:19.095 --> 00:05:20.845
I want to keep moving forward
we got more work to do.

00:05:20.845 --> 00:05:22.268
We got more lives to change.

00:05:22.268 --> 00:05:23.160
It's the process.

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:24.830
It's not just hitting
a million subscribers.

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:27.511
I could do that a lot faster

00:05:27.511 --> 00:05:29.058
and a lot easier doing other things.

00:05:29.058 --> 00:05:32.020
You know, if I was bashing entrepreneurs.

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:34.011
Bashing celebrities.

00:05:34.011 --> 00:05:36.369
Saying all the negative things about them.

00:05:36.369 --> 00:05:38.641
That would actually draw
a lot more attention.

00:05:38.641 --> 00:05:40.191
I would get a lot more subscribers.

00:05:40.191 --> 00:05:42.774
That's the sad state of humans.

00:05:44.417 --> 00:05:46.344
We'd rather attack
somebody then embrace them

00:05:46.344 --> 00:05:48.053
and learn from them.

00:05:48.053 --> 00:05:50.253
We'd rather escape from
a life that we don't like

00:05:50.253 --> 00:05:52.927
as opposed to try and build
a life that we do like.

00:05:52.927 --> 00:05:55.042
And that's fine.

00:05:55.042 --> 00:05:56.140
But I don't want to do that.

00:05:56.140 --> 00:05:57.240
I would never be great at that.

00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:58.740
I don't like bashing people.

00:05:58.740 --> 00:06:01.057
I don't want to show the
negative sides of everybody.

00:06:01.057 --> 00:06:02.929
'Cause everybody has a negative side.

00:06:02.929 --> 00:06:05.285
It's not what I want
to put up to the world.

00:06:05.285 --> 00:06:07.721
And so my only goal is I want
to hit a million subscribers

00:06:07.721 --> 00:06:10.362
and I'll do anything I can to get there.

00:06:10.362 --> 00:06:11.785
Those are the kind of
things I would be doing

00:06:11.785 --> 00:06:12.961
but I'd never be great at them.

00:06:12.961 --> 00:06:15.202
And I could never get to that goal.

00:06:15.202 --> 00:06:17.803
Because that's not who I am.

00:06:17.803 --> 00:06:19.630
It's cause I don't enjoy the process.

00:06:19.630 --> 00:06:21.899
And so not everything
is going to be amazing.

00:06:21.899 --> 00:06:23.088
There's a lot of crap
that you have to deal with

00:06:23.088 --> 00:06:24.428
as an entrepreneur.

00:06:24.428 --> 00:06:27.189
But if you just make it about the goal

00:06:27.189 --> 00:06:29.220
and just hitting that mark

00:06:29.220 --> 00:06:30.604
then you're never going to get there

00:06:30.604 --> 00:06:32.597
and you'll really have to focus on

00:06:32.597 --> 00:06:33.532
whether you're a writer,

00:06:33.532 --> 00:06:34.588
whether you're a singer,

00:06:34.588 --> 00:06:35.563
whether you're a dancer,

00:06:35.563 --> 00:06:36.903
whether you're a Youtuber.

00:06:36.903 --> 00:06:37.920
Whatever it is.

00:06:37.920 --> 00:06:41.782
You're a software developer,
you have to enjoy writing code.

00:06:41.782 --> 00:06:44.303
You have to enjoy the process
of figuring things out

00:06:44.303 --> 00:06:45.805
and solving the problems.

00:06:45.805 --> 00:06:48.162
And not just hitting a revenue target.

00:06:48.162 --> 00:06:49.749
I think when you can do that.

00:06:49.749 --> 00:06:53.608
When you can tie your
self worth into the work.

00:06:53.608 --> 00:06:56.493
And say I'm proud of
this thing that I made.

00:06:56.493 --> 00:06:58.117
Even if nobody else likes it.

00:06:58.117 --> 00:06:59.825
This has been a lot of
videos that I put up

00:06:59.825 --> 00:07:01.570
that you guys haven't liked.

00:07:01.570 --> 00:07:02.750
That we've killed.

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:04.135
I'm still proud of them.

00:07:04.135 --> 00:07:05.674
I still love them.

00:07:05.674 --> 00:07:09.212
I was still like I am so
happy that I made that video.

00:07:09.212 --> 00:07:12.623
I think it's great, it's genius.

00:07:12.623 --> 00:07:13.802
But it didn't work.

00:07:13.802 --> 00:07:16.358
So it's great, so it's good
for a certain amount of people.

00:07:16.358 --> 00:07:18.590
It's good for me and a select few.

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:20.539
I can't build a business around it.

00:07:20.539 --> 00:07:22.938
But I don't feel bad
about creating a series

00:07:22.938 --> 00:07:25.216
that was a sinker, it was a loser.

00:07:25.216 --> 00:07:26.600
Like that's a great piece of content.

00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:28.143
I'm insanely proud of it.

00:07:28.143 --> 00:07:31.031
And I think that as long as
you are insanely proud daily

00:07:31.031 --> 00:07:32.941
of the work that you are creating.

00:07:32.941 --> 00:07:35.547
And some of them are going to hit.

00:07:35.547 --> 00:07:36.888
And some of them are going to miss.

00:07:36.888 --> 00:07:38.472
In fact most of them are going to miss.

00:07:38.472 --> 00:07:41.279
You're going to fail way more
then you're going to be a success.

00:07:41.279 --> 00:07:43.066
But if you're proud of
the work and the hustle

00:07:43.066 --> 00:07:44.772
that you're putting in daily.

00:07:44.772 --> 00:07:47.538
Then you're not just getting
more self worth for yourself

00:07:47.538 --> 00:07:50.133
and feel better about what
you're doing every day.

00:07:50.133 --> 00:07:52.246
But eventually if you stick
with it, you'll get a career

00:07:52.246 --> 00:07:55.212
and amazing business
that'll have a big impact

00:07:55.212 --> 00:07:56.962
on the rest of the world.

00:07:56.962 --> 00:07:58.016
So the question of the day today

00:07:58.016 --> 00:08:02.099
is, I'm curious, does or
did your mom support you

00:08:03.048 --> 00:08:05.767
in what you're doing right now?

00:08:05.767 --> 00:08:07.310
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:08:07.310 --> 00:08:08.367
I'm really curious to find out.

00:08:08.367 --> 00:08:10.727
I just want to give a quick
shout out to Shahrukh Hasan.

00:08:10.727 --> 00:08:12.675
Shahruhk thank you so
much for picking up a copy

00:08:12.675 --> 00:08:15.641
of my book, Your One Word,
and taking that awesome,

00:08:15.641 --> 00:08:19.011
exciting picture and
posting it to your Twitter.

00:08:19.011 --> 00:08:20.755
I love the joy on your face.

00:08:20.755 --> 00:08:24.707
Thank you so much for the
support and for enjoying my book.

00:08:24.707 --> 00:08:25.931
So thank you guys so much for watching.

00:08:25.931 --> 00:08:27.634
I believe in you.

00:08:27.634 --> 00:08:29.339
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:08:29.339 --> 00:08:31.456
and whatever your one word is.

00:08:31.456 --> 00:08:33.976
Much love and I'll see
you again tomorrow morning

00:08:33.976 --> 00:08:36.819
for another shot of Entspresso.

00:08:36.819 --> 00:08:39.829
♫ I wake up every morning.

00:08:39.829 --> 00:08:43.496
♫ Entspresso keep me going.

00:08:46.561 --> 00:08:48.884
- Every pursuit, no matter
how glamorous it may seem,

00:08:48.884 --> 00:08:51.409
no matter how exciting it feels to you,

00:08:51.409 --> 00:08:53.610
no matter how much you were born to do it,

00:08:53.610 --> 00:08:55.438
comes with a shit sandwich.

00:08:55.438 --> 00:08:58.854
And so the question is not what do I love.

00:08:58.854 --> 00:09:00.558
The question is what do I love so much

00:09:00.558 --> 00:09:02.443
that I don't mind eating the shit sandwich

00:09:02.443 --> 00:09:04.108
that comes along with that thing.

00:09:04.108 --> 00:09:07.245
So for me and my life, writing
is the thing that I love.

00:09:07.245 --> 00:09:09.158
And the shit sandwich was the seven years

00:09:09.158 --> 00:09:10.830
that I was not getting published.

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:12.985
And that I was coming home from my job

00:09:12.985 --> 00:09:15.703
as a diner waitress, as a
bartender, as an au pair,

00:09:15.703 --> 00:09:18.427
as somebody who worked in
flea markets, as a cook.

00:09:18.427 --> 00:09:19.772
And I was coming home tired

00:09:19.772 --> 00:09:21.398
and smelling like other
people's french fries.

00:09:21.398 --> 00:09:23.552
And sitting down and doing my real job.

00:09:23.552 --> 00:09:25.015
Which was to write.

00:09:25.015 --> 00:09:27.456
And then to go to the
mail box the next day

00:09:27.456 --> 00:09:29.038
and get another rejection letter.

00:09:29.038 --> 00:09:31.480
And then say, do I still want to do this?

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:33.350
'Cause this shit sandwich sucks.

00:09:33.350 --> 00:09:34.651
(laughter)

00:09:34.651 --> 00:09:36.237
- Am I ready to take another bite?

00:09:36.237 --> 00:09:38.067
- And I did still want to do it.

00:09:38.067 --> 00:09:41.483
And now even as somebody who
makes their living as a writer.

00:09:41.483 --> 00:09:42.662
There's no end to the shit sandwiches.

00:09:42.662 --> 00:09:47.051
It's like, oh hello horrible
review in prominent newspaper.

00:09:47.051 --> 00:09:49.280
That's your shit sandwich today Liz.

00:09:49.280 --> 00:09:50.333
You still want to do this work?

00:09:50.333 --> 00:09:52.572
Yeah I still do, still worth it.

00:09:52.572 --> 00:09:55.661
Like hello awful comment on social media

00:09:55.661 --> 00:09:59.766
from somebody who thinks
you're a pile of dog shit.

00:09:59.766 --> 00:10:00.864
(laughter)

00:10:00.864 --> 00:10:02.786
You know and just like
chosen every possible way,

00:10:02.786 --> 00:10:05.227
that they just cannot get it
out of their system fast enough

00:10:05.227 --> 00:10:07.705
how much disregard they
have for your entire life.

00:10:07.705 --> 00:10:09.575
Still want to do this thing?

00:10:09.575 --> 00:10:10.835
Yeah I still want to do it.

00:10:10.835 --> 00:10:12.216
So that's the question.

00:10:12.216 --> 00:10:13.762
Because if the first time

00:10:13.762 --> 00:10:15.310
you encounter the shit
sandwich you're like,

00:10:15.310 --> 00:10:18.033
well this isn't worth it.

00:10:18.033 --> 00:10:20.589
Then that's not the thing
you're supposed to be doing.

00:10:20.589 --> 00:10:23.149
And there are plenty of
things in life that I have run

00:10:23.149 --> 00:10:26.274
into the shit sandwich and
been like so not worth it.

00:10:26.274 --> 00:10:27.494
(laughter)

00:10:27.494 --> 00:10:29.765
So not worth it, like this is
not, I don't want to do this.

00:10:29.765 --> 00:10:33.623
Like whatever the alleged
benefits of this thing might be.

00:10:33.623 --> 00:10:34.456
No, this whole cycle, no.

00:10:34.456 --> 00:10:35.945
(laughter)

00:10:35.945 --> 00:10:39.149
You know, like I know it's
probably really good for me

00:10:39.149 --> 00:10:40.614
but I feel like throwing up right now

00:10:40.614 --> 00:10:41.996
cause this is too hard.

00:10:41.996 --> 00:10:43.790
You'll not be seeing me here again.

00:10:43.790 --> 00:10:46.876
You know, and I love my
sisters at Soul Cycle.

00:10:46.876 --> 00:10:48.784
I just don't like feeling
like I'm going to throw up.

00:10:48.784 --> 00:10:49.617
When I exercise.

00:10:49.617 --> 00:10:50.980
So it's not for me.

00:10:50.980 --> 00:10:53.742
And so that's the question.

00:10:53.742 --> 00:10:55.451
So if you go into this thing thinking,

00:10:55.451 --> 00:10:58.738
if I follow my bliss, and I live my dream,

00:10:58.738 --> 00:11:02.005
and I stand in my truth, that
everything will be great.

00:11:02.005 --> 00:11:04.370
It doesn't mean everything will be great.

00:11:04.370 --> 00:11:05.712
It just means at the end of the day

00:11:05.712 --> 00:11:07.091
when you check in with yourself

00:11:07.091 --> 00:11:10.999
and you go, in the end, on the balance,

00:11:10.999 --> 00:11:13.353
is this still better than not doing it?

00:11:13.353 --> 00:11:15.261
And the answer is still yeah
this thing's still better

00:11:15.261 --> 00:11:17.698
than not doing it, then
you're on the right path.

00:11:17.698 --> 00:11:19.405
- I knew I wanted to be
in the skate industry.

00:11:19.405 --> 00:11:20.342
I loved skating too much.

00:11:20.342 --> 00:11:21.481
I wanted to be in it.

00:11:21.481 --> 00:11:22.539
I didn't know if I would make a living

00:11:22.539 --> 00:11:26.075
as a professional, but I was
going to be, I was devoted

00:11:26.075 --> 00:11:27.294
to skateboarding so.

00:11:27.294 --> 00:11:30.961
I refinanced my house
and took all the money

00:11:32.478 --> 00:11:33.643
and started a skateboard company.

00:11:33.643 --> 00:11:35.833
Which seems like the stupidest
thing in the world to do

00:11:35.833 --> 00:11:37.581
when skating's dying but,

00:11:37.581 --> 00:11:40.309
it was exactly what I wanted to do.

00:11:40.309 --> 00:11:42.586
I wanted to be a company
owner, be behind the scenes.

00:11:42.586 --> 00:11:44.294
I quit my sponsor and started

00:11:44.294 --> 00:11:48.683
and for about three years
struggled very hard.

00:11:48.683 --> 00:11:53.006
With, my partner and I we had
pooled our money together.

00:11:53.006 --> 00:11:54.091
He was an ex pro skater as well.

00:11:54.091 --> 00:11:56.258
And we just did Birdhouse.

00:11:57.689 --> 00:12:00.029
Did whatever we could to get by

00:12:00.029 --> 00:12:03.020
and all the team was staying on my couch.

00:12:03.020 --> 00:12:04.269
Literally like while I'm changing diapers,

00:12:04.269 --> 00:12:06.586
I'm like driving guys to these spots

00:12:06.586 --> 00:12:08.414
that they're going to get arrested at.

00:12:08.414 --> 00:12:10.558
Because there's no skate parks

00:12:10.558 --> 00:12:12.304
so they're going to go ride school yards

00:12:12.304 --> 00:12:15.601
and (laughing) it was
such a strange existence.

00:12:15.601 --> 00:12:18.656
But I loved it, because
it was skateboarding

00:12:18.656 --> 00:12:19.870
and it was exactly what I wanted to do.

00:12:19.870 --> 00:12:23.691
And so, we really hunkered down you know.

00:12:23.691 --> 00:12:27.185
I was living on Taco Bell
and peanut butter jelly.

00:12:27.185 --> 00:12:28.018
And Top Ramen.

00:12:28.018 --> 00:12:28.851
- [Interviewer] Mmm.

00:12:28.851 --> 00:12:31.851
- For probably three years for sure.

00:12:32.766 --> 00:12:34.155
But I didn't care 'cause
it was like I still got

00:12:34.155 --> 00:12:35.120
to do what I love.

00:12:35.120 --> 00:12:36.418
That's the thing is that people think,

00:12:36.418 --> 00:12:37.251
was it a struggle?

00:12:37.251 --> 00:12:41.010
Well no, because I loved it too much.

00:12:41.010 --> 00:12:42.674
I still got to go skate.

00:12:42.674 --> 00:12:43.607
And I had time to skate.

00:12:43.607 --> 00:12:45.964
I didn't have to go sit behind
a computer for eight hours

00:12:45.964 --> 00:12:48.199
and then hope I get time to skate.

00:12:48.199 --> 00:12:50.763
- I've never been interested
in living a balanced life.

00:12:50.763 --> 00:12:53.614
I think that balanced people
don't change the world,

00:12:53.614 --> 00:12:54.447
first of all.

00:12:54.447 --> 00:12:57.194
I think balanced people
don't really follow a dream.

00:12:57.194 --> 00:12:59.755
This doesn't mean that you
don't have responsibilities.

00:12:59.755 --> 00:13:01.097
Like just go to the other
part of this question,

00:13:01.097 --> 00:13:02.116
how can you have a family.

00:13:02.116 --> 00:13:03.336
Well sure you can have a family.

00:13:03.336 --> 00:13:07.725
But balance is kind of
like, I feel like balance

00:13:07.725 --> 00:13:10.575
is like a made up word, it's
like invented by corporations.

00:13:10.575 --> 00:13:13.054
You know to make their employees
think that they're happy.

00:13:13.054 --> 00:13:14.440
It's like you've got this balance.

00:13:14.440 --> 00:13:16.346
Like you could work at Microsoft you know

00:13:16.346 --> 00:13:17.485
or something here in Seattle.

00:13:17.485 --> 00:13:19.410
- [Interviewer] There's
like 10 Microsoft people

00:13:19.410 --> 00:13:20.243
in the audience here.

00:13:20.243 --> 00:13:21.076
- No disrespect to Microsoft.

00:13:21.076 --> 00:13:22.893
Let's pick another company,
Microsoft's a great company.

00:13:22.893 --> 00:13:23.852
- [Interviewer] One out of
every five people in Seattle

00:13:23.852 --> 00:13:24.709
works at Microsoft.

00:13:24.709 --> 00:13:28.487
- That's right you know, and
it's like you got this thing.

00:13:28.487 --> 00:13:29.668
And maybe you love your job.

00:13:29.668 --> 00:13:31.093
And if you love your job that's great.

00:13:31.093 --> 00:13:32.799
But I hear from a lot
of dissatisfied people

00:13:32.799 --> 00:13:34.466
at these big companies and they write in

00:13:34.466 --> 00:13:36.375
and they're like I'm reading
your blog from my cubicle

00:13:36.375 --> 00:13:39.463
and I have this good job,
I have my health insurance,

00:13:39.463 --> 00:13:42.230
I've got free yoga every Thursday.

00:13:42.230 --> 00:13:44.343
But I'm not really, you know,

00:13:44.343 --> 00:13:45.176
- [Interviewer] Fulfilled.

00:13:45.176 --> 00:13:46.132
- Right, I'm not really fulfilled.

00:13:46.132 --> 00:13:47.608
So for me I guess I'm much more interested

00:13:47.608 --> 00:13:48.441
in that word fulfilled.

00:13:48.441 --> 00:13:50.232
How can you live a fulfilled life?

00:13:50.232 --> 00:13:53.446
You can live a fulfilled life
and still pay your bills.

00:13:53.446 --> 00:13:54.872
Lots of creative people do it.

00:13:54.872 --> 00:13:57.922
Lots of unconventional people do it.

00:13:57.922 --> 00:13:59.651
I would say if anything it's
actually much more common now

00:13:59.651 --> 00:14:00.871
than it used to be.

00:14:00.871 --> 00:14:04.954
When I first started
working online 15 years ago,

00:14:05.815 --> 00:14:08.170
I didn't know a lot of other
people who were doing that.

00:14:08.170 --> 00:14:10.528
My friends thought I was
selling drugs or something.

00:14:10.528 --> 00:14:11.384
- [Interviewer] Well you were (laughing).

00:14:11.384 --> 00:14:14.024
- Well I was, you know, but,
or like online gambling.

00:14:14.024 --> 00:14:15.773
Or you know whatever,
like parents have no idea

00:14:15.773 --> 00:14:16.606
how the internet works.

00:14:16.606 --> 00:14:18.859
But now it's much more common.

00:14:18.859 --> 00:14:21.543
So I don't really like
the word balance myself.

00:14:21.543 --> 00:14:23.409
- [Interviewer] So what we'd like to do

00:14:23.409 --> 00:14:25.360
is we'd like to replace the word.

00:14:25.360 --> 00:14:28.782
Like living a balanced
life is not the goal.

00:14:28.782 --> 00:14:31.022
The goal is living a fulfilled life.

